1. Create Firebase project in Firebase console
2. Add iOS and Android apps to the Firebase project
3. Install Firebase dependencies: `npx expo install @react-native-firebase/app @react-native-firebase/auth @react-native-firebase/firestore @react-native-firebase/storage`
4. Configure Firebase initialization in app startup:
   ```typescript
   import { initializeApp } from 'firebase/app';
   import { getAuth } from 'firebase/auth';
   import { getFirestore } from 'firebase/firestore';
   import { getStorage } from 'firebase/storage';

   const firebaseConfig = {
     apiKey: '...',
     authDomain: '...',
     projectId: '...',
     storageBucket: '...',
     messagingSenderId: '...',
     appId: '...'
   };

   const app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);
   export const auth = getAuth(app);
   export const db = getFirestore(app);
   export const storage = getStorage(app);
   ```
5. Create Firebase service wrappers for auth, database, and storage operations
6. Set up security rules for Firestore and Storage
7. Configure offline persistence for Firestore
8. Implement error handling and retry logic for Firebase operations

